Name: COMPASS_2010_I843494
Year: 2010
Summary: Proton virtual-photon asymmetry in 160 GeV polarized muon DIS
Experiment: COMPASS
Collider: CERN SPS fixed target
InspireID: 843494
Status: UNVALIDATED
Reentrant: true
Authors:
 - Andreas Papaefstathiou <apapaefs@kennesaw.edu>
References:
 - Phys.Lett.B 690 (2010) 466-472
RunInfo: Requires independent mu+p samples for PP, PM, MP, and MM helicities.
NumEvents: 100000
NeedsCrossSection: yes
Beams: [[ANTIMUON, p+]]
Energies: [[160.0, 0.938272]]
Description:
  Reconstructs finite-muon-mass fixed-target DIS kinematics from the
  highest-energy prompt outgoing positive muon, excluding leptons from
  hadron decays.
  The selection is Q2 > 1 GeV2, 0.1 < y < 0.9, and 0.004 < x < 0.7;
  no unreported W cut is imposed. Fixed 160 GeV generation approximates the
  published beam-momentum window. R1998 is used in D; eta*A2 is neglected
  and g2 is not modeled when constructing A1 from four physical helicity
  samples.
